e biden administration offered  billions in subsidies to a taiwanese  company if it agrees not to sell its  most advanced semiconductor chips to  china  taiwan semiconductor manufacturing  company makes the most advanced chips  for nearly every company on earth  including nvidia in amd  although tsmc has factories in china and  one in the us its most advanced  factories are in taiwan for security  reasons i did a video about the  importance of tsmc which i'll link in my  description  tsmc is now building a 12 billion dollar  factory in arizona so it's no surprise  that arizona's governor doug ducey is  the latest american politician to cozy  up to taiwan he flew there to meet with  taiwanese president tai engwin  not to mention in 2019 the trump  administration lobbied the dutch  government to block the shipment of  cutting-edge machines that are an  essential component in printing chips  for tsmc and other chip makers the dutch  firm asml is the only company in the  world making the 150 million dollar  machines that pattern the finest lines  on the most advanced ships  the biden administration has been  pushing asml to stop shipping even its  less sophisticated systems to china  which would seriously hurt chinese firms  that are producing their own  semiconductor chips  these new u.s restrictions involving  nvidia and amd are another attempt to  hamper china's technological  capabilities without integrated units  from these two companies chinese firms  will find it more difficult to implement  advanced computing for speech and image  recognition  these processes are commonly found in  smartphones for example for identifying  people in photos on your iphone  they also have military uses  such as scouring satellite imagery for  weapons or military bases  or listening to communications and  monitoring faces for intelligence  gathering purposes  washington has argued that products sold  in the chinese marketplace are ending up  in the hands of the chinese military  for example nvidia in intel sold ships  to sugan a chinese firm that makes  computers for various companies but also  supplies them to the chinese military a  report in 2020 by the new york times  raised concerns that these chips are  powering a supercomputing center that  conducts mass surveillance in china's  northwest xinjiang province to track  uighurs and other muslim minorities  both intel and nvidia told the times  they were unaware of what they called  the misuse of their technology  in 2016 a chinese police surveillance  project called sharp eyes had the  ambitious plan of being able to monitor  a hundred percent of all public spaces  in china by 2020 even the vast rural  areas  there is no word on how far they've come  in achieving this goal  although the blockade is meant to  prevent american technology from being  used by america's military rival ai  chips have wide applications companies  like alibaba baidu and tencit use them  in their data centers to process large  volumes of data  now they'll have to make do with lower  performance gpus that could slow them  down  so there are broader implications for  society  or perhaps it is inevitable that china  will begin producing its own high-end  gpus and become self-reliant  it may only be a matter of time  the people who are shaping our future  have a deep understanding of how the  world works which is why brushing up on  your math science and computer science  skills is essential that's why i trust  brilliant which helps you improve your  stem skills through learning  interactively i know my viewers  especially love their computer science  fundamentals course in this course you  have to deliver mail to every house on  the street using as few commands as  possible  you can solve puzzles with science  through their scientific thinking course  or practice everyday math by seeing  numbers in a new light there's something  for everyone for me i'm continuing to  enjoy their logic courses which are  helping to improve my critical thinking  skills  there are no tests in brilliantness for  people of all experience levels whether  you're a student or already working it's  free for you to try out if you head to  the custom link in my description  brilliant.org slash newsthink and the  first 200 people who sign up with my  link will get 20 off brilliant annual  premium subscription which gives you  access to all of the offerings including  the most advanced courses  thanks so much for watching for  newsthink i'm cindy palm
 

